===Critical response===
The [[review aggregator]] website [[Rotten Tomatoes]] reported an 86% approval rating with an average rating of 9.1/10 based on 7 reviews.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Marvel's Cloak & Dagger: Season 2 (2019) |url=https://www.rottentomatoes.com/tv/marvel_s_cloak_and_dagger/s02 |access-date=May 24, 2019 |website=[[Rotten Tomatoes]] |publisher=[[Fandango Media]]}}</ref>

''[[/Film]]''{{'}}s Monique Jones gave the second season a "B−", saying that the first season had a stronger sense of direction.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Jones |first=Monique |date=May 31, 2019 |title='Cloak And Dagger' Ends Its Uneven Second Season With A Satisfying Cliffhanger |url=https://www.slashfilm.com/566785/cloak-and-dagger-season-2-finale-review/ |access-date=October 14, 2025 |website=[[/Film]] |language=en-US}}</ref> Samantha Nelson of ''[[The Verge]]'' critiqued season 2's use of a "ridiculous, well-worn supervillain trope".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Nelson |first=Samantha |date=March 27, 2019 |title=Cloak & Dagger’s power creep is a problem for season 2 |url=https://www.theverge.com/2019/3/27/18284279/cloak-and-dagger-season-2-review-marvel-superheroes-aubrey-joseph-olivia-holt |access-date=October 14, 2025 |website=[[The Verge]] |language=en-US}}</ref> ''[[ComicBook.com]]''{{'}}s Charlie Ridgely gave the season 5/5 stars, praising the show's ability to tackle real-world issues such as police brutality and human trafficking.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ridgely |first=Charlie |date=June 4, 2019 |title='Marvel's Cloak & Dagger' Season 2 Review: Still the Most Important Superhero Series on the Air |url=https://comicbook.com/marvel/news/marvels-cloak-and-dagger-season-2-review/ |access-date=October 14, 2025 |website=[[ComicBook.com]] |language=en-US}}</ref>

